BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 641.70 Tm (Slide 1 - Opening) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 624.70 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 611.60 Tm (Good morning respected judges, teachers, and everyone here. We are presenting SAHAYAK, a real-time) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 599.50 Tm (    Indian Sign Language recognition prototype. Our project explores how a camera and a computer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 587.40 Tm (    program may help recognize a limited set of trained signs. We will explain the problem, show) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 575.30 Tm (    how our prototype works, and talk honestly about what it can and cannot do.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 558.20 Tm (Show: the homepage and the project name. Pause, look at the judges, and introduce the team.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 536.10 Tm (Slide 2 - The communication challenge) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 519.10 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 506.00 Tm (People who use sign language may find it hard to communicate with someone who does not understand) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 493.90 Tm (    their signs. This can happen in classrooms, public places and daily conversations. Technology) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 481.80 Tm (    may help in some situations, but it must be designed carefully and tested with the people who) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 469.70 Tm (    may use it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 452.60 Tm (Indian Sign Language is a full language. It has its own rules and ways of showing meaning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 440.50 Tm (    Recognizing a few hand signs is not the same as understanding a full conversation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 418.40 Tm (Slide 3 - Why accessibility matters) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 401.40 Tm (Optional fact: The 2011 Census of India counted 5,071,007 people in its hearing-disability) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 389.30 Tm (    category. This is an old census figure. It is not the number of ISL users and it is not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 377.20 Tm (    current estimate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 360.10 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 347.00 Tm (This figure shows that hearing accessibility is an important topic, but we must not confuse) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 334.90 Tm (    hearing-disability figures with the number of people who use ISL. Our project explores one) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 322.80 Tm (    small part of a much bigger issue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 305.70 Tm (Source: https://censusindia.gov.in/nada/index.php/catalog/43369/) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 292.60 Tm (For current global hearing-loss information, check:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 280.50 Tm (    https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/deafness-and-hearing-loss) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 258.40 Tm (Slide 4 - What SAHAYAK does) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 241.40 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 228.30 Tm (SAHAYAK uses a camera to see a hand pose or movement. The website finds key points on the hand and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 216.20 Tm (    changes those points into numbers. A trained model uses the numbers to guess one of the signs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 204.10 Tm (    it has learned. The website then displays the predicted label as text.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 187.00 Tm (A landmark is a key point on the hand, such as a fingertip or joint. A model learns patterns from) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 174.90 Tm (    examples that have labels. It does not understand a sign exactly as a person does.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.05 0.30 0.55 rg 1 0 0 1 42 152.80 Tm (Slide 5 - Goal and limits) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 135.80 Tm (Say:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 122.70 Tm (Our goal is to show a working path from camera input to a predicted sign label. The current system) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 110.60 Tm (    supports a limited set of trained signs. It is not a complete ISL translator and cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 98.50 Tm (    replace a qualified interpreter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 81.40 Tm (The website also has extra speech and translation features, but not every feature works offline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.22 rg 1 0 0 1 42 69.30 Tm (    Results can change with lighting, camera angle, hidden hands, movement and differences between) Tj ET
